wlines. So we use \\n in the JSON value. That will be interpreted as newline by JSON parser. So the above string is correct.\n\nThus final JSON object.\n\nI'll output it without any extra whitespace, just the JSON.\n\nNote: The first and last characters must be brace.\n\nI'll produce:\n\n{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    segs = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    n = len(segs)\\n    names = [s['name'] for s in segs]\\n    importance = [s['importance'] for s in segs]\\n    minimum = [s['minimum'] for s in segs]\\n    capacity = [s['capacity'] for s in segs]\\n    total_min = sum(minimum)\\n    total_cap = sum(capacity)\\n    if budget < total_min or budget > total_cap:\\n        raise ValueError('Budget out of feasible range')\\n    alloc = list(minimum)\\n    remaining = budget - total_min\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_idx = -1\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            if alloc[i] < capacity[i]:\\n                if best_idx == -1:\\n                    best_idx = i\\n                else:\\n                    left = importance[i] * (alloc[best_idx] + 1)\\n                    right = importance[best_idx] * (alloc[i] + 1)\\n                    if left > right or (left == right and i < best_idx):\\n                        best_idx = i\\n        if best_idx == -1:\\n            break\\n        alloc[best_idx] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    total = sum(alloc)\\n    by_name = {names[i]: alloc[i] for i in range(n)}\\n    return {'allocations': alloc, 'by_name': by_name, 'total': total}\"}\n\nDouble-check: the string has a newline after each \\n. That's fine.\n\nBut note: the Python code includes a line `raise ValueError('Budget out of feasible range')` with parentheses and single quotes. That's fine.\n\nAlso ensure that the function signature is exactly `def solve(case):`. Yes.\n\nNow output."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1496,"completion_tokens":3786,"total_tokens":5282,"prompt_tokens_de